# A take-off in a wartime twin: lining up to five hundred feet.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **Every speed here is the aeroplane own.** The Mosquito rotates at about 121
# knots and climbs at about 148, against a Cessna 56 and 75, so a figure
# written as a number would be meaningless across the two. `rotate` and
# `climb` come from `assets/figures/mosquito-fb6.xml` through
# `sim::departure_speeds`.
#
# **The swing on take-off is what this class is about.** A Merlin twin at full
# power swings, and the Notes say so; the attitude band below catches an
# aeroplane hauled off or held down, and the heading is the pilot own to keep
# straight because a lesson that named a runway heading would only suit one
# runway.

# **Keeping her straight is watched, because it is the first thing a take-off
# asks for and nothing here used to ask it.** A Mosquito once swung forty-five
# degrees off the centreline on its roll and its lesson said nothing, because
# it watched the throttle, the rotation speed, the attitude and the climbing
# speed and not the heading. Flown properly the five aeroplanes taught a
# take-off swing between 1.1 and 11.1 degrees, so twenty degrees is that with
# room - wide enough for honest technique in a tail-wheel aeroplane, and
# nowhere near wide enough to miss a swing off the runway.

name Take-off in a wartime twin
teaches second-world-war

stage The roll
do Line up, then open the throttles slowly and evenly to full
do Hold her straight on the rudder: she will swing as the power comes in
do Let the speed build to the rotation speed. Do not hurry her off
hold lesson/turned-deg -20 20 Keep her straight on the take-off roll
need fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.90 Open the throttles fully for the take-off
need velocities/vc-kts >= rotate-5 Let her reach the rotation speed before easing the nose up
until position/h-agl-ft >= 15

stage The initial climb
do Hold the climbing attitude and let the speed settle
do Raise the undercarriage once there is no runway left to land on
hold attitude/theta-deg -8.0 24.0 Hold the climbing attitude
until position/h-agl-ft >= 200

stage Climbing away
do Climb straight ahead at the climbing speed
hold velocities/vc-kts climb-70 climb+70 Hold the climbing speed
until position/h-agl-ft >= 500
